# hashes2 — HINCRBY and HDEL
#
# Learn: HINCRBY key field n adds to one numeric field atomically, the
# same way INCRBY does for a whole string key. HDEL removes fields.
#
# Task: the check seeds user:7 (with a visits field) and the shopping
# cart cart:7 (field = product, value = quantity). Record one more visit,
# add 2 more of sku:42 to the cart, and remove sku:13 from the cart
# entirely. The values differ between runs, so no hard-coded numbers.
#

HSET user:7 visits 4
HSET cart:7 sku:42 3
HSET cart:7 sku:13 0
